{"game": "remnant-2", "language": "english", "appid": 1282100, "month": "2025-09", "window": 4, "start_date": 1758585600, "end_date": 1759276799, "month_true_total": 242, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-12 14:57:05 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "205578816", "author": {"steamid": "76561198449312474", "personaname": "waboofjnr", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198449312474/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 56, "playtime_forever": 1230, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 285, "last_played": 1761759381, "avatar": "d5afaeea5a39eacc3e5ab7a039a7b740f0b89341"}, "language": "english", "review": "No sense of \"earning victory\" or genuinely getting better at the game like something like Dark Souls, which I had hoped there would be - most boss fights (every one that I faced) had the same sense of just getting lucky with the attacks or mob spawns. Map system has a cool \"red if not discovered\" mechanic but is otherwise super confusing with no indicators of where to head, and different floors of the same area are super hard to look how to get into or out of.\n\nMelee is impossible with the amount of stamina you are given - and, since there are no parries or actual true you-to-enemy stun, you just die in a few hits on Veteran. \"Melee\" class with the shotgun is abysmal, and not worth even accidentally glancing over with your mouse.\n\nAll in all, it's lacking the sense of achievement you can find in heaps over at Bandai Namco, and is probably top contender for \"shoot it and hope it dies before you get stun-locked or killed by off-screen enemies\" 2025.", "timestamp_created": 1759273891, "timestamp_updated": 1759273891, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.453463345766067505", "comment_count": 1, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "205575112", "author": {"steamid": "76561197977199539", "personaname": "Corin93", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561197977199539/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 32, "playtime_forever": 149, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 149, "last_played": 1759269149, "avatar": "f2daf1b11462c0ded2352e5e1e667efcbed10a56"}, "language": "english", "review": "Repetitive combat is tedious", "timestamp_created": 1759269234, "timestamp_updated": 1759269234, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.455104559659957886", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "205574557", "author": {"steamid": "76561198067165163", "personaname": "Scouter N00B [NO SOUND]", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198067165163/", "num_games_owned": 124, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 5089, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2246, "last_played": 1783602082, "avatar": "a0fb05c4300f7dc9f627bc4f44012ab71033c257"}, "language": "english", "review": "Worth Every Penny. Can easily sink couple of hundred hours with build variety and RNG World reroll. A great successor to Remnant From the Ashes. I played Remnant from Ashes (the prequel to this game) free from Epic. It was a real sleeper. Did not expect the game would be that good. Got this one for discount on Steam. Worth every penny and then some more. Definitely worth a buy even at full cost including all DLCs (since each DLC comes with a new class aka. What the game calls Archetype'.", "timestamp_created": 1759268617, "timestamp_updated": 1759268617, "voted_up": true, "vo